      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T17:11:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are the requirements for the serialization here? This encoding is more verbose than what you were previously using, but it includes the curve.\n\nDepending on what you want, including the curve is either a benefit or a risk.\n\nIf, at the point you parse the input, you don\u0027t know the key type out-of-band, it\u0027s helpful to have it in-band. But then you need to reason through what happens if the input contains a key type you didn\u0027t expect.\n\nIf, at that point, you already know the key type, this is just a waste of bytes and adds risks when if you parse something of the wrong type and break internal invariants.\n\nSince this CL is missing the parsing half, I can\u0027t be sure of this. (Though I also don\u0027t have the cycles to fully review your cryptographic design. This is also why, per the comment below, why we (BoringSSL team) will not support code like this and instead will be requiring teams use the official bindings.)",
      "revId": "7cea90c8946cc6658d7075bf53d8f2797b3801b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
