      "writtenOn": "2023-09-15T08:21:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the explanation. Yes, I do want to parse the key and use it for signing later. In go/avf-rkpvm-keyblob \u003e Background, I have described the generation and usage scenario of this private key.\n\nApart from that, the doc described the management of the private key generated here. The key is generated and encrypted, then is passed to rkpd. Later we retrieve the encrypted key blob from rkpd, decrypt it and use it to sign. The retrieval process requires a different set of APIs, which have not been implemented yet. My plan is to add these APIs around November.\n\nActually in the first PS I didn\u0027t take any format, because my main intention was to verify that the generation of the key pair works smoothly with the integration of boringssl.",
      "parentUuid": "febad49b_aafb33cf",
      "revId": "7cea90c8946cc6658d7075bf53d8f2797b3801b2",
