      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T17:11:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function should be marked unsafe, no? Otherwise you can, in safe code, take a garbage pointer, wrap it in `Buffer::new` and then use `as_slice` to get a bad slice out of it.\n\nNot only that, a bad pointer will cause `drop` to break things. So actually you have a lot of safety requirements. `ptr` must have been allocated by `OPENSSL_malloc` (or be null; see below), and `len` bytes from it must be valid and initialized. And then also `new` takes ownership of the buffer. None of that is documented.",
      "revId": "7cea90c8946cc6658d7075bf53d8f2797b3801b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
