      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T17:11:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `out_len \u003e 0` check is a memory leak. If you initialize a `CBB` with non-zero initial capacity, then don\u0027t write anything to it, we will return you a buffer with length zero but allocated buffer.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "7cea90c8946cc6658d7075bf53d8f2797b3801b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9acc233b_d3eb97b8",
        "filename": "rialto/src/requests/ec_key.rs",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1031048
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T17:11:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This null check is also off, but it is slightly complicated. In C, (null, 0) is a perfectly valid representation of the empty buffer. This differs from Rust, where it isn\u0027t. Rust, unfortunately, made a mistake and made decisions that make it very unsafe to use with FFI. This is part of why we\u0027re making our own crate in BoringSSL. We do not support teams calling into BoringSSL bindgen output like this, so code like this really should be working with us. Unfortunately, Android Rust isn\u0027t \n\nIf you initialize a `CBB` with zero capacity, it\u0027s perfectly valid for BoringSSL to return (null, 0). I think it actually won\u0027t right now, but the API contract is you must tolerate it.\n\nI think the thing to is drop all the null and zero-length checks here and in `Buffer::new`. Instead, `as_slice` should special-case zero-length slices.\n\nSome context on where Rust messed this up: https://groups.google.com/a/google.com/g/unsafe-rust-crabal/c/42XI6HuDvcU\n\nOr use `Vec` as previously suggested, and then you don\u0027t need to spread it across so many places. 😊",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "7cea90c8946cc6658d7075bf53d8f2797b3801b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
